the double child killer colin pitchfork  has been arrested and recalled to prison  just two months after his release after  breaching conditions of his license  pitchfork was jailed for life in 1988  for raping and strangling to 15 year old  girls in leicestershire well our  correspondent aisha saheed is here in  the studio and aisha  just remind us a little bit of the  background to this case and why he's  been recalled to prison so quickly after  fighting for his release well it's not  quite clear what exactly happened he was  released on 40 license conditions  and he must have breached one or  potentially more of them to be recalled  this early  now if we look at what exactly happened  he was given a life sentence in 1988 for  raping and strangling two  fifteen-year-olds linda mann and dawn  ashworth in leicestershire in 1983 and  1986 respectively and following his  arrest in 1987 he was the first man to  be convicted for murder based on dna  evidence he received a life sentence  with a 30-year minimum term his minimum  term was reduced by two years in 2009  and despite two denied requests for  parole one in 2016 and the other in 2018  he was deemed suitable for release in  march this year he was let go with as i  said more around 40 license conditions  in september and today we've learned  he's been recalled back to prison most  likely for breaching one if not more of  these conditions now his release earlier  this year was a highly contentious one  that in june the justice secretary at  the time robert buckland asked for the  parole board to re-examine their  decision they rejected this government  challenge which mr buckland said he was  disappointed by but he respected their  decision  and the big question is what happens now  it's likely that pitchfork will spend a  substantial amount of time in prison  within 28 days the parole board will  have to make a decision a formal review  on what to do with him it's likely they  will call for a full hearing where they  decide whether he is kept in an open  prison in a closed prison or whether he  is released and if he is kept in prison  there won't be another option  opportunity for a parole review until  mid-2023  aisha thanks very much
 

